 "findings": [
  {
   "evidence": "Mathlib's SmoothFunctions.lean has `coe_mul` but no sum/prod evaluation lemma (grep `theorem (coe_sum|coe_prod|sum_apply|prod_apply)` in Mathlib/Geometry/Manifold/Algebra finds only `coe_mul`). `evalRingHom` is defined at SmoothFunctions.lean:221 as `(Pi.evalRingHom _ m).comp ContMDiffMap.coeFnRingHom`, so the `change` and the `rfl` both depend on unfolding that definition.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Geometry/Manifold/Algebra/VanishingIdeal/Pow.lean",
   "fix": "Add evaluation lemmas such as `ContMDiffMap.sum_apply`/`prod_apply` (or `evalRingHom_apply`) and rewrite with them plus `ContMDiffMap.comp_apply` and `hc`, or at minimum comment the `change` and replace the `rfl` with `simp [hc]`.",
   "issue": "`hPy` is proved by an uncommented `change ContMDiffMap.evalRingHom y P = _`, then `simp only [P, map_sum, map_mul, map_prod]` and a closing `rfl`. That `rfl` silently relies on `evalRingHom` unfolding to pointwise evaluation, on `((a r).comp F) y` reducing to `a r (F y)`, and on `c (r j) y` unfolding, all through the `ContMDiffMap` wrappers.",
   "line": 151
  }
 ],
